Fix java:S1206 - override hashCode() alongside equals()

StockKeepingUnit overrides equals(Object) but inherits Object.hashCode(),
so two equal instances can report different hash codes. That breaks the
equals/hashCode contract and makes the type unusable as a HashMap key or
HashSet element.

The fix is additive: it introduces hashCode() derived from exactly the same
fields equals() compares (code, warehouse). No existing method is touched,
so no observable behaviour changes.

Rule: https://rules.sonarsource.com/java/RSPEC-1206

diff --git a/src/main/java/com/example/demo/StockKeepingUnit.java b/src/main/java/com/example/demo/StockKeepingUnit.java
--- a/src/main/java/com/example/demo/StockKeepingUnit.java
+++ b/src/main/java/com/example/demo/StockKeepingUnit.java
@@ -33,5 +33,10 @@
         }
         return Objects.equals(code, that.code)
                 && Objects.equals(warehouse, that.warehouse);
     }
+
+    @Override
+    public int hashCode() {
+        return Objects.hash(code, warehouse);
+    }
 }
